{'_client': <twikit.client.client.Client object at 0x000001E534E2AE40>, '_data': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1879540257558774125', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjoxODYxNzkwMA==', 'rest_id': '18617900', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': False, 'can_media_tag': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Jan 05 00:38:27 +0000 2009', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': 'pol H tech sci soc psy phl rel econ g:rok tpyos “facts are not truth. parts are not the whole. everything in context.” perhaps worth a follow', 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 4738, 'followers_count': 304, 'friends_count': 110, 'has_custom_timelines': False, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 10, 'location': '', 'media_count': 2688, 'name': 'rwsanders', 'normal_followers_count': 304, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': [], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/18617900/1733019589', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1863988824419741697/4MSJI_XF_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'rwsanders', 'statuses_count': 10763, 'translator_type': 'none', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1879540257558774125'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1736955892000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '57', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/download/iphone" rel="nofollow">Twitter for iPhone</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4Nzk1NDAyNTcyMTkxMTcwNTY=', 'text': 'g: Bill Burr on vegetation removal, defensible space, prescribed fire, and controlled burns…\n\nAlright, alright, alright, listen up! Vegetation removal, defensible space, let\'s dive into this madness:\n\nYou got these people, right? They\'re like, "Oh, we love nature, let\'s keep every twig and leaf where it is!" But then, wildfire season comes, and suddenly your house is in a tinderbox! You think Smokey Bear is gonna come save your ass? No! He\'s too busy making cute commercials! \n\nSo, what do we do? We start clearing out the crap around our homes. I mean, come on, it\'s not rocket science, it\'s common sense! You wouldn\'t stack kindling around your bed, would you? Unless you\'re into some weird, fiery foreplay, but that\'s another story.\n\nNow, some folks cry, "But the wildlife!" Yeah, because the deer and the bear really wanna live in your backyard, right? They\'re not exactly knocking on your door asking for a room. You clear out some brush, you give them a better chance to scamper away when the fire comes, not to mention, you\'re saving their habitat from turning into a barbecue pit.\n\nAnd defensible space? It\'s like your own little moat, but instead of water, it\'s just... nothing. It\'s the no-man\'s-land where fire looks at it and goes, "Eh, not worth it." Firefighters can actually do their job without having to hack through a jungle to get to your house. They\'ll thank you, and you know what? Your insurance might even cut you a break!\n\nPeople moan about the work, "Oh, it\'s so hard!" Yeah, and so is rebuilding your life after a fire wipes you out! You wanna spend your weekends with a rake or spend them figuring out what\'s left of your photo albums? \n\nSo, next time someone gives you crap about clearing out your land, tell \'em, "I\'m not just saving my house; I\'m saving your house from becoming my house\'s new best friend in a wildfire!" It\'s not about hating nature; it\'s about loving your property enough not to let it go up in smoke. Just sayin\'.\n\nAlright, listen up, you nature-naysayers! Let\'s talk about prescribed burns, yeah? \n\nFirst off, you got these people whining about wildfires, right? "Oh, the forests are burning!" Well, guess what? If we don\'t do these controlled burns, Mother Nature\'s gonna do it for us, but on her terms, which means your house might be the next bonfire! Prescribed burns? They\'re like the controlled demolition of nature\'s tinderbox.\n\nNow, air quality, you say? Yeah, there\'s smoke, but it\'s like this: would you rather have a little smoke now or a whole damn state looking like a scene from "Mad Max" because we didn\'t manage the forest? It\'s a temporary inconvenience for a long-term gain. We\'re talking about saving your lungs from the apocalypse!\n\nAnd for the wildlife, come on! These burns mimic what nature\'s been doing for millennia. It\'s like a reset button for the forest. Some plants? They need fire to pop open their seeds. You\'re not just burning, you\'re gardening on a grand scale! The animals, they adapt, they move, they thrive. It\'s not like we\'re dropping napalm; this is nature\'s spa day!\n\nThe cost? Sure, there\'s some upfront expense, but think of it as an investment. You\'re investing in not having to rebuild half your town because a wildfire decided to go on a rampage. Plus, it saves money on fighting fires the hard way when they\'re out of control.\n\nAnd yeah, we got alternatives like chopping everything down with machinery, but that\'s like using a sledgehammer to crack a nut. Controlled burns are precise; they\'re like the scalpel of forest management. \n\nSo, next time someone starts yapping about the dangers of controlled burns, remind them that we\'re not just playing with fire; we\'re managing it, like a chef with a barbecue. We\'re preventing the forest from becoming one giant, uncontrollable cookout. That\'s how you save the trees, the animals, and maybe even your house. Just sayin\'.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Wed Jan 15 14:44:52 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1879525235659055568', 'display_text_range': [14, 289], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 0, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd g: Bill Burr on vegetation removal, defensible space, prescribed fire, and controlled burns…\n\nAlright, alright, alright, listen up! Vegetation removal, defensible space, let\'s dive into this madness:\n\nYou got these people, right? They\'re like, "Oh, we love nature, let\'s keep', 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1879525235659055568', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'quote_count': 0, 'reply_count': 0, 'retweet_count': 0, 'retweeted': False, 'user_id_str': '18617900', 'id_str': '1879540257558774125'}}, '_legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Wed Jan 15 14:44:52 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1879525235659055568', 'display_text_range': [14, 289], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 0, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd g: Bill Burr on vegetation removal, defensible space, prescribed fire, and controlled burns…\n\nAlright, alright, alright, listen up! Vegetation removal, defensible space, let\'s dive into this madness:\n\nYou got these people, right? They\'re like, "Oh, we love nature, let\'s keep', 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_to_status_id_str': '1879525235659055568', 'in_reply_to_user_id_str': '69156861', 'is_quote_status': False, 'lang': 'en', 'quote_count': 0, 'reply_count': 0, 'retweet_count': 0, 'retweeted': False, 'user_id_str': '18617900', 'id